 ## Background
-Boolean operations on SDFs were popularized in the context of ray marching and procedural graphics by Inigo Quilez and others in the early 2010s [S11, S13, unofficial]. The technique leverages the mathematical property that the signed distance function to a union of sets is the minimum of their individual distance functions, and the intersection is the maximum [S4, unofficial][S8]. It is a fundamental building block for [Constructive SDF Modeling (Min Combination)](871-constructive-sdf-modeling-min-combination.md) and allows for the creation of complex scenes from simple primitives like spheres and boxes [S2, S6, unofficial].
